      "image": "assets/story-ethan-leo-c01-s02-va95d72732eb2.webp",
      "imageAlt": "Ethan and Leo explore a dusty basement filled with cobwebbed shelves, old jars, tools, and boxes.",
      "caption": "The brothers descend into a basement crowded with forgotten things.",
      "text": "The stairs groaned under their weight as Ethan and Leo crept downward, each step sounding louder than it should in the silence of the house. The flashlight beam wavered in Ethan’s hand, cutting through the gloom in narrow slices. The deeper they went, the colder the air became, heavy with the smell of damp stone and rust. It was the kind of chill that seemed to seep into bones, whispering of places where sunlight had never reached.\n\nLeo moved quickly, his sneakers squeaking against the wood, his excitement bubbling over. He glanced back at Ethan with a mischievous grin. “Feels like we’re descending into a dungeon,” he said, his voice echoing off the walls. “All we need now is a dragon.”\n\nEthan rolled his eyes, though his heart thumped harder. “More like rats,” he muttered. “Or mold. Or something worse.”\n\nThe beam of light swept across shelves sagging under jars filled with nails, rusted tools, and boxes marked in their grandfather’s faded handwriting. Dust floated in the air like tiny ghosts, disturbed by their movement. A cobweb brushed against Ethan’s arm, and he flinched, shaking it off quickly.\n\nLeo darted ahead, kicking aside a pile of newspapers that crumbled into fragments. “Smells like something died down here,” Ethan said, wrinkling his nose.\n\n“Or something’s waiting to be found,” Leo shot back, his voice bouncing against the stone walls. He spread his arms wide, as if embracing the darkness. “This is perfect. It’s like the start of every great adventure.”\n\nEthan tightened his grip on the flashlight, sweeping it across the room. The shadows seemed to shift, stretching and curling, as though alive. He swallowed hard. “Just… don’t touch anything yet. We don’t know what’s down here.”\n\nLeo laughed, bounding down the last few steps. “That’s the point, Ethan. We’re supposed to find out.”\n\nThe basement swallowed them whole, the storm fading into a distant murmur above. For the first time, Ethan realized how far away the world felt — as though the two of them had crossed into another place entirely, one filled with secrets waiting to be uncovered."
