      "imageAlt": "Leo rests a reassuring hand on Ethan's shoulder as Ethan holds the map and journal in their boat near the rocky island.",
      "caption": "Leo's confidence helps Ethan choose courage despite the warning ahead.",
      "text": "The boat rocked steadily as the brothers drifted closer to the cliffs, the sea whispering against the hull. Ethan sat hunched over the map, his brow furrowed, his fingers tracing the spiral again and again. The ink seemed to curl endlessly, pulling his thoughts into its depths. His chest tightened, unease gnawing at him.\n\n“What if this leads us into danger?” he said at last, his voice low, almost swallowed by the sound of the waves. His eyes flicked toward the cliffs, their jagged edges rising like teeth. “Grandpa’s warning wasn’t just words. He knew something. He wanted us to be careful.”\n\nLeo leaned back, his grin unwavering, though his eyes softened. “Danger’s part of the adventure,” he said, his tone brimming with defiance. “Every great story has risk. That’s what makes it worth telling.” He tapped the oar against the side of the boat, the sound sharp and certain. “If we turn back now, we’ll never know what’s waiting.”\n\nEthan’s gaze dropped to the journal resting beside him. The words beware the signs echoed in his mind, heavy and insistent. He wanted to believe in the treasure, in the adventure, but fear pressed against him like a weight. He thought of the safety of home, the quiet of familiar walls, the certainty of ordinary life. And yet… the stars above glittered, the map pulsed with secrets, and the island loomed ahead like destiny itself.\n\nLeo leaned forward, his grin softening into something steadier, more resolute. “We’ll face it together,” he said firmly. “Whatever comes, we’ll handle it. You and me.”\n\nThe silence stretched between them, heavy but binding. Ethan exhaled slowly, his shoulders sagging. He looked at his brother — fearless, determined, unshakable — and felt the bond between them tighten. “We’ll follow it,” he whispered. “Together.”\n\nThe words hung in the air, sealing their resolve. The boat rocked onward, the cliffs looming closer, the spiral etched into their minds. Doubt lingered, but resolve burned brighter. The journey was no longer just about discovery. It was about courage — and the strength of two brothers bound by choice."
