      "imageAlt": "Ethan holds a glowing map whose bright trail points toward the island as Leo pauses at the oar beneath a brilliant dawn sky.",
      "caption": "The map finally reveals one clear trail leading straight to the mysterious island.",
      "text": "The stormy omen had passed, leaving the sea restless but calmer, its waves rolling like heavy breaths. Ethan steadied the map against the lantern’s glow, his fingers trembling as he aligned the parchment with the stars above. He tilted it carefully, tracing the spirals and jagged lines until suddenly — as if the ink itself shifted — the symbols revealed their secret.\n\nHis breath caught. The scattered marks were no longer fragments; they formed a trail, a path winding across the parchment and pointing toward a single destination. Ethan’s eyes widened, his voice breaking into a whisper. “It’s there… the island.”\n\nLeo froze mid-stroke, the oars dripping saltwater as he turned to look. His grin spread slowly, triumph burning in his eyes. “The island,” he repeated, his voice fierce with certainty. “That’s where the treasure waits.”\n\nThe revelation hung between them, heavy and undeniable. The map had spoken, the stars had confirmed, and the horizon itself seemed to shimmer with promise. Ethan’s heart pounded, torn between awe and dread. The journal’s warning echoed in his mind — not all symbols lead to treasure — but the trail was too clear, too deliberate to ignore.\n\nThe cliffs loomed larger, their jagged edges catching the dawn light. The island rose from the sea like a sentinel, its shadow stretching long across the waves. Ethan felt the weight of destiny pressing against him, the realization that they were no longer wandering — they were being led.\n\nLeo dipped the oars back into the water, his grin unshakable, his strokes strong and sure. “We’ve found it,” he said, his voice brimming with triumph. “Grandpa’s secret. His legacy. It’s waiting for us.”\n\nEthan clutched the map tighter, his knuckles pale. The revelation burned in his chest, both exhilarating and terrifying. The stars glittered above, the island loomed ahead, and the spiral’s path had brought them here.\n\nThe journey was no longer about searching. It was about claiming."
