      "imageAlt": "Leo bounds joyfully across the island beach while Ethan walks carefully with the rolled map and their boat rests by the shore.",
      "caption": "Ethan and Leo take their first steps onto the island at sunrise.",
      "text": "The island rose from the horizon like a sleeping giant, its jagged cliffs catching the first light of dawn. Mist clung to its edges, curling upward like smoke, as though the land itself exhaled secrets. The brothers’ patched boat creaked as it cut through the waves, each stroke of Leo’s oars pulling them closer to the unknown.\n\nEthan sat rigid, the map spread across his knees, his eyes darting between the parchment and the looming cliffs. The spirals and jagged lines had led them here, converging on this place with undeniable precision. His chest tightened as he whispered, almost to himself, “This is it. The island.”\n\nLeo’s grin widened, his voice carrying over the crash of waves. “We made it! Can you feel it, Ethan? Adventure’s waiting for us.” His eyes gleamed, reflecting the rising sun, his spirit unshaken by doubt.\n\nThe boat scraped against the shallows, the sound sharp and final. Ethan jumped out first, his boots sinking into wet sand. The air was heavy with salt and something else — a faint, earthy musk that spoke of age and mystery. He scanned the shoreline: twisted trees leaned toward the water, their roots clawing at the sand, while dark caves yawned at the base of the cliffs.\n\nLeo leapt onto the shore, arms spread wide as though claiming the land. “Our island,” he declared, his voice triumphant. He turned to Ethan, his grin unshakable. “Grandpa’s secrets are here. I know it.”\n\nEthan’s gaze lingered on the caves, unease gnawing at him. The journal’s warning echoed in his mind: Not all who seek will return. He swallowed hard, his throat dry. “We need to be careful,” he said firmly. “This place feels… alive.”\n\nThe wind picked up, rustling the twisted trees, carrying with it a sound that was almost a whisper. The island seemed to watch them, its silence heavy, its secrets buried deep.\n\nTogether, the brothers stood on the shore, the boat behind them, the cliffs ahead. They had crossed the threshold. The island had accepted them — or trapped them."
