      "image": "assets/story-ethan-leo-c04-s03-vdef9ced881a5.webp",
      "imageAlt": "Ethan studies the map while Leo lights spiral and starburst carvings with a torch just inside a wet cave entrance.",
      "caption": "The brothers leave the bright shore and follow matching symbols into the caves.",
      "text": "The shoreline gave way to the looming cliffs, their jagged faces scarred by time and tide. At the base of the cliffs, dark openings yawned like mouths, each cave promising secrets and shadows. The air grew cooler as the brothers approached, the salty tang of the sea replaced by a damp, earthy musk that clung to their skin.\n\nEthan slowed his steps, his boots crunching against the sand as he stared into the nearest cave. Its entrance was wide, but the darkness inside was absolute, swallowing the light of dawn. He felt a chill crawl up his spine, the journal’s warning echoing in his mind: Beware the signs. He tightened his grip on the map, his voice low and uneasy. “Leo… these caves feel wrong. Like they’re waiting for us.”\n\nLeo’s grin flickered but did not fade. He stepped closer, his eyes gleaming with excitement. “Waiting means there’s something inside,” he said, his tone brimming with defiance. He picked up a piece of driftwood, lit it with the lantern, and held it high. The flame sputtered, casting long shadows across the cave walls. “Adventure doesn’t hide in the sunlight. It hides in places like this.”\n\nThe brothers stepped inside, the sound of the sea fading behind them. The cave walls were slick with moisture, etched with faint markings that shimmered under the torchlight. Ethan leaned closer, his breath catching. Symbols — spirals, jagged lines, starbursts — carved into the stone itself. His chest tightened. “The same as the map,” he whispered. “Grandpa’s clues are here too.”\n\nLeo’s grin widened, triumphant. “Then we’re exactly where we’re supposed to be.” He ran his fingers across the carvings, tracing the spirals with reverence. “This isn’t just a cave. It’s part of the puzzle.”\n\nThe deeper they walked, the narrower the passage became, the shadows pressing closer. The air grew colder, heavy with silence, broken only by the drip of water echoing through the stone. Ethan’s cautious nature gnawed at him, his heart pounding with unease. The cave felt alive, its walls watching, its symbols whispering secrets too old to understand.\n\nLeo’s fire burned beside him, fearless and unshaken. “We’ll solve it,” he said firmly, his voice echoing against the stone. “Whatever Grandpa left here, we’ll find it.”\n\nEthan swallowed hard, his throat dry. The cave had accepted them, or trapped them. Either way, the brothers had crossed another threshold. The shoreline was behind them, the darkness ahead. The journey had shifted once again — no longer just about following the map, but about surviving the island’s tests."
