      "imageAlt": "Ethan and Leo pause to listen in a wet tunnel where blue spiral reflections ripple across the carved walls and puddles.",
      "caption": "Mysterious echoes and glowing ripples seem to guide them farther underground.",
      "text": "The cave swallowed them whole, its darkness pressing in from every side. The flickering torchlight cast long, jagged shadows across the stone walls, making the carvings seem to twist and move. The deeper they went, the more the silence thickened, heavy and suffocating, broken only by the drip of water echoing through the cavern.\n\nEthan slowed his steps, his boots crunching against loose gravel. His breath came shallow, his chest tight. Then he heard it — faint at first, like a whisper carried on the damp air. A sound that didn’t belong to the sea or the stone. He froze, his hand tightening around the map. “Leo,” he whispered, his voice trembling. “Do you hear that?”\n\nLeo stopped, his grin faltering as he tilted his head. The sound grew clearer — a low murmur, repeating, bouncing off the walls. It wasn’t words, not exactly, but it carried rhythm, like voices caught in the stone itself. His eyes widened, though determination burned in them. “Echoes,” he said firmly, his voice echoing back at him. “The cave is speaking.”\n\nThe torchlight flickered, illuminating spirals carved deeper into the walls. Ethan stepped closer, his fingers brushing the grooves. The echoes grew louder, resonating with the carvings, as though the stone itself was alive. His stomach twisted. “It’s not just sound,” he murmured. “It’s… a warning. Or a guide.”\n\nLeo’s grin returned, fierce and defiant. “Then we follow it,” he said, his voice steady. He raised the torch higher, the flame sputtering but holding, casting light deeper into the passage. “Grandpa left us this trail. The echoes are part of it.”\n\nThe brothers pressed on, the echoes surrounding them, growing louder with each step. Ethan’s cautious nature screamed at him to turn back, but the map pulsed in his hands, the spirals glowing faintly under the torchlight. The cave seemed to breathe, its whispers guiding them deeper, its shadows watching.\n\nThe echoes were no longer just sound. They were a presence, a force woven into the stone, testing their resolve. Ethan swallowed hard, his throat dry, his heart pounding. “We’re being led,” he whispered. “Or trapped.”\n\nLeo’s fire blazed beside him, fearless and unshaken. “Either way,” he said, his grin unyielding, “we keep going.”\n\nTogether, they stepped deeper into the cave, the echoes rising around them like a chorus, binding them to the island’s secrets."
