      "chapter": "The Trial",
      "section": "Chapter 4: The Island",
      "chapterNumber": 4,
      "sceneNumber": 8,
      "image": "assets/story-ethan-leo-c04-s08-v22ca6ae832cf.webp",
      "imageAlt": "Ethan presses one hand to a bright turquoise spiral while Leo raises his torch and the guardian watches from the glowing chamber wall.",
      "caption": "Ethan and Leo meet the guardian's challenge with caution, courage, and trust.",
      "text": "The chamber trembled as the guardian’s shadow loomed larger, its presence pressing against the brothers like a storm contained within stone. The glowing symbols pulsed in rhythm with the figure, spirals twisting, jagged lines crackling, starbursts shimmering like constellations alive. The air grew heavy, charged with energy, each breath thick and difficult.\n\nEthan’s heart pounded, his grip on the map tightening until his knuckles turned white. The journal’s warning echoed louder than ever: Beware the signs. He swallowed hard, his voice trembling. “Leo… this is the trial. Grandpa didn’t just leave clues. He left a test.”\n\nLeo’s grin flickered but did not fade. His eyes gleamed with defiance, his voice steady. “Then we pass it. That’s what we’re here for.” He stepped forward, raising the torch high. The flame sputtered but held, casting light across the guardian’s shadow.\n\nThe figure shifted, its eyes glowing brighter, its form stretching taller. The chamber roared with silence, the hum deepening into a sound that shook the stone. The carvings flared, their light blinding, their patterns shifting into alignment with the map. Ethan’s chest tightened, fear gnawing at him. The trial was not a puzzle to solve — it was a confrontation.\n\nThe guardian’s shadow moved, its presence pressing closer, its voice rumbling through the chamber though no words were spoken. Ethan felt it in his bones, a demand, a challenge. He clutched the map tighter, his breath shallow. “It wants us to prove ourselves,” he whispered. “Not with the map. With courage.”\n\nLeo’s fire blazed beside him, fearless and unshaken. He stepped forward, his voice ringing out against the stone. “We’re not afraid,” he declared. “We’ve come too far to turn back.”\n\nThe chamber shook, the symbols flaring brighter, the guardian’s shadow looming closer. Ethan’s fear pressed against him, but Leo’s determination burned stronger, binding them together. The trial had begun — not of knowledge, but of resolve.\n\nThe brothers stood side by side, one with caution, the other with courage, facing the guardian’s shadow. The island had awakened its test, and the journey was no longer about discovery. It was about proving they were worthy to claim the secrets buried within."
