      "imageAlt": "Ethan and Leo discover a black stone altar glowing with spiral symbols in a hidden cavern room.",
      "caption": "A hidden altar waits at the heart of the island's memory.",
      "text": "The whispers faded into silence, leaving the chamber heavy with anticipation. The torchlight flickered across the stone until the passage narrowed again, spiraling downward into a hidden recess. Ethan’s breath caught, his chest tightening, the map glowing faintly in his hands. He swallowed hard, his voice trembling. “Leo… there’s something ahead. Something the island has kept secret.”\n\nThe corridor opened suddenly into a chamber smaller than the others, but its presence was overwhelming. At its center stood an altar — carved from black stone, etched with spirals and jagged lines that pulsed faintly with light. The air was thick, charged with energy, carrying the hum that had followed them since the labyrinth. Ethan froze at the threshold, awe and dread mingling. “It’s the altar,” he whispered. “The heart of the island’s memory.”\n\nThe altar shimmered faintly, its carvings glowing brighter as they approached. Shadows bent with the torchlight, stretching long across the chamber. Ethan clutched the map tighter, its ink pulsing in rhythm with the altar. His chest tightened, his breath shallow. “It’s not just stone,” he murmured. “It’s alive. It’s… waiting for us.”\n\nLeo’s grin softened, replaced by reverence. He raised the torch higher, its flame sputtering but holding, casting light across the altar. “Then this is the trial’s end,” he said firmly, his voice steady. “The hidden altar is the key. Grandpa wanted us to find this.”\n\nThe chamber roared with silence, the altar pulsing brighter, its spirals twisting deeper, its jagged lines sparking faintly. Ethan’s cautious nature screamed at him to retreat, but the altar demanded their presence, its glow pressing closer. He swallowed hard, his voice trembling. “It’s asking for something,” he murmured. “Not just courage. A choice. A sacrifice.”\n\nThe map shimmered violently, its ink glowing in harmony with the altar. Ethan’s heart pounded, fear gnawing at him, but beside him Leo’s fire blazed, fearless and unbroken.\n\nThe hidden altar was not just stone. It was memory, demand, destiny. The brothers stood together, bound by the map, bound by the stars, bound by the trials they had endured.\n\nThe journey had shifted once again — no longer just about discovery, but about unlocking the island’s deepest secret, hidden in the altar’s glow."
