      "imageAlt": "Ethan and Leo place their glowing map together above the spiral-lit altar.",
      "caption": "The brothers choose to offer the map together rather than sacrifice one another's trust.",
      "text": "The hidden altar pulsed with light, its spirals glowing brighter, its jagged lines sparking faintly. The chamber roared with silence, the air heavy, charged with energy. Ethan froze at the threshold, his chest tightening, the map glowing violently in his hands. He swallowed hard, his voice trembling. “Leo… it’s asking for something. A gift. An offering.”\n\nThe altar shimmered, its carvings twisting deeper, its glow pressing closer. Shadows bent with the torchlight, stretching long across the stone. Ethan’s cautious nature screamed at him to retreat, but the altar demanded their presence, its hum vibrating through the chamber, through their bones.\n\nLeo stepped forward, his grin gone, replaced by reverence. He raised the torch higher, its flame sputtering but holding, casting light across the altar. “Then this is the trial’s end,” he said firmly, his voice steady. “The offering is the key. Grandpa wanted us to face this.”\n\nThe map pulsed violently, its ink shimmering in rhythm with the altar. Ethan clutched it tighter, his knuckles pale, his chest tight. “It’s not just asking for courage,” he murmured. “It’s asking for sacrifice. Something we value most.”\n\nThe chamber trembled, the altar glowing brighter, its spirals twisting into new shapes. Ethan’s stomach twisted, his throat dry. He thought of the shoreline, the boat, the safety they had left behind. He thought of the treasure, the promise of everything they had dreamed. His voice broke. “What if it wants the map?”\n\nLeo’s fire blazed beside him, fearless and unbroken. He stepped closer to the altar, his voice ringing out against the stone. “Then we give it. If that’s the price, we pay it. We didn’t come here to keep secrets. We came here to uncover them.”\n\nThe altar pulsed, its glow pressing closer, demanding. Ethan’s heart pounded, fear gnawing at him, but he looked at his brother — determined, unyielding — and felt the bond between them tighten. He exhaled slowly, his voice a whisper. “Together,” he said. “We make the offering together.”\n\nThe brothers stepped forward, the altar shimmering brighter, the chamber trembling, the island’s secrets pressing closer. The offering was not just sacrifice. It was unity, destiny, resolve.\n\nThe journey had shifted once again — no longer just about discovery, but about surrendering something precious to unlock the island’s deepest truth."
