      "text": "The chamber lay in silence after the verdict, the altar’s glow softening, the spirals fading into a steady rhythm like a heartbeat. Ethan’s chest loosened, his breath coming easier, though his hands still trembled around the map. The Keeper’s shadow lingered, its eyes no longer burning with judgment but shimmering with calm.\n\nEthan swallowed hard, his voice breaking. “Leo… it’s not leaving. It’s waiting.”\n\nThe Keeper’s presence pressed closer, but the weight of its gaze had changed. No longer heavy with trial, it carried something else — a quiet reverence, a promise. The altar pulsed gently, its jagged lines sparking faintly, its spirals glowing brighter.\n\nLeo stepped forward, his fire blazing, his voice steady. “Then this is the gift. The island has chosen us. The Keeper is offering something.” He raised the torch higher, its flame sputtering but holding, casting light across the altar.\n\nThe shadows bent with the torchlight, stretching long across the chamber. The altar shimmered, its carvings twisting into new shapes. Slowly, deliberately, a compartment opened at its center. Within lay a stone tablet, etched with spirals and starbursts, glowing faintly with the same rhythm as the map. Ethan’s breath caught, awe and dread mingling. “It’s… another map,” he whispered. “Or a key.”\n\nThe Keeper’s eyes glowed brighter, its presence pressing closer, urging them forward. Ethan’s cautious nature screamed at him to retreat, but the gift demanded their presence, its glow pressing closer. His chest tightened, his throat dry. “It’s meant for us,” he murmured. “But only if we accept it.”\n\nLeo’s fire blazed beside him, fearless and unbroken. He stepped to the altar, his voice ringing out against the stone. “Then we take it. Together.”\n\nThe brothers reached forward, their hands brushing the glowing tablet. The altar pulsed violently, the chamber trembling, the Keeper’s shadow looming taller. For a moment, Ethan thought the stone would consume them, but then the glow softened, flowing into their hands, into the map, into their very bones.\n\nThe Keeper’s eyes dimmed, its shadow fading, its presence dissolving into silence. The altar shimmered one final time before settling into stillness.\n\nEthan’s breath caught, his voice breaking. “Leo… it gave us the key. The Keeper’s gift. The island’s secret is ours to carry.”\n\nLeo’s grin returned, fierce and unyielding. He lowered the torch, his voice steady. “Then the journey isn’t ending. It’s beginning. The gift is the path forward.”\n\nThe brothers stood together, bound by the map, bound by the stars, bound by the Keeper’s gift.\n\nThe journey had shifted once again — no longer just about surviving trials, but about carrying the island’s truth into the depths beyond."
